fig8 M,T then trefoil M,T => {"st2":"Trefoil: mirror +3","st3":{"readout":"Sum +3Right-handed","seen":"Trefoil: mirror +3","label":"Trefoil, mirrored and turned over. Marks plus, plus, plus. Sum plus 3, right-handed.","revealBtn":{"text":"Show me why","disabled":null},"pressed":"Turn over:true Mirror:true Trefoil:true:dis Figure-eight:false","phase":"explore"},"reveal":"Your prediction held.\n\nTurning the mirrored trefoil over left every mark plus: turning over is a way of moving it, so its hand stayed right. Mirroring turned every mark plus, and no wiggling gets back: the trefoil is not its own mirror image, as Max Dehn proved in 1914.\n\nThe figure-eight's marks summed to 0 both ways, and it is its own mirror image. So a trefoil comes in a left and a right version, and turning one over never swaps them.","errors":[]}
